      "end_time": 1.675,
      "duration": 1.675,
      "phoneme_count": 13
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "sentence": "Today we have for you:",
      "paragraph_id": 0,
      "word_count": 5,
      "start_time": 1.675,
      "end_time": 3.75,
      "duration": 2.075,
      "phoneme_count": 20
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "sentence": "A sheet-pan chicken dinner for apple season",
      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "word_count": 7,
      "start_time": 3.75,
      "end_time": 7.0,
      "duration": 3.25,
      "phoneme_count": 41
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "sentence": "New-crop applesauce",
      "paragraph_id": 2,
      "word_count": 2,
      "start_time": 7.0,
      "end_time": 9.1,
      "duration": 2.1,
      "phoneme_count": 18
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "sentence": "And a beautiful fall salad with apples, Cheddar and crispy sage (did we mention we have apple recipes today?)",
      "paragraph_id": 3,
      "word_count": 19,
      "start_time": 9.1,
      "end_time": 17.15,
      "duration": 8.05,
      "phoneme_count": 112
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "sentence": "What does the start of apple season make you think of?",
      "paragraph_id": 4,
      "word_count": 11,
      "start_time": 17.15,
      "end_time": 20.725,
      "duration": 3.575,
      "phoneme_count": 53
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "sentence": "Is it the buttery, caramelized scent of an apple pie wafting from the oven?",
      "paragraph_id": 4,
      "word_count": 14,
      "start_time": 20.725,
      "end_time": 26.25,
      "duration": 5.525,
      "phoneme_count": 75
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "sentence": "Or do you daydream about going apple picking, filling baskets with red, yellow and green fruit?",
      "paragraph_id": 4,
      "word_count": 16,
      "start_time": 26.25,
      "end_time": 32.95,
      "duration": 6.7,
      "phoneme_count": 94
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "sentence": "For me, it\u2019s the first bite of a new-crop apple, crisp as a celery stick, nearly as juicy as a peach and bracingly tangy.",
      "paragraph_id": 4,
      "word_count": 24,
      "start_time": 32.95,
      "end_time": 41.925,
      "duration": 8.975,
      "phoneme_count": 123
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "sentence": "It also immediately brings to mind a moment in the classic Beverly Cleary kids\u2019 series \u201cRamona.\u201d Ramona Quimby, the 4-year-old protagonist, hides in the basement from her big sister, Beezus, who is supposed to be minding her, and takes exactly one bite of each new-season apple in a crate she finds, tossing the apples aside as she goes.",
      "paragraph_id": 5,
      "word_count": 58,
      "start_time": 41.925,
      "end_time": 65.525,
      "duration": 23.6,
      "phoneme_count": 346
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "sentence": "When Beezus is scandalized, Ramona is ready with an irrefutable response: \u201cBut the first bite tastes best.\u201d",
      "paragraph_id": 6,
      "word_count": 17,
      "start_time": 65.525,
      "end_time": 73.9,
      "duration": 8.375,
      "phoneme_count": 113
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "sentence": "Unruffled, their mother uses the despoiled apples to make a very large batch of applesauce.",
      "paragraph_id": 7,
      "word_count": 15,
      "start_time": 73.9,
      "end_time": 80.55,
      "duration": 6.65,
      "phoneme_count": 89
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "sentence": "And Ramona is so contrite that she eats all her carrots at dinner without complaint.",
      "paragraph_id": 7,
      "word_count": 15,
      "start_time": 80.55,
      "end_time": 86.3,
      "duration": 5.75,
      "phoneme_count": 84
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "sentence": "Since I first read that book as a kid, I think of Ramona every time I take the first bite of a new apple.",
      "paragraph_id": 8,
      "word_count": 24,
      "start_time": 86.3,
      "end_time": 93.9,
      "duration": 7.6,
      "phoneme_count": 112
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "sentence": "Then, of course, I finish it because the entire apple\u2019s awfully good.",
      "paragraph_id": 8,
      "word_count": 12,
      "start_time": 93.9,
      "end_time": 98.975,
      "duration": 5.075,
      "phoneme_count": 66
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "sentence": "So what\u2019s your favorite part of apple season?",
      "paragraph_id": 9,
      "word_count": 8,
      "start_time": 98.975,
      "end_time": 102.125,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "phoneme_count": 45
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "sentence": "Let me know at hellomelissa@nytimes.com.",
      "paragraph_id": 9,
      "word_count": 5,
      "start_time": 102.125,
      "end_time": 105.675,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "phoneme_count": 44
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "sentence": "In the meantime, I\u2019ll be using some of my best apples to make Colu Henry\u2019s sheet-pan chicken with apples, fennel and onions, in which fruit and fowl are seasoned with fennel and rosemary.",
      "paragraph_id": 10,
      "word_count": 33,
      "start_time": 105.675,
      "end_time": 118.525,
      "duration": 12.85,
      "phoneme_count": 183
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "sentence": "It\u2019s a savory salute to a crisp and redolent season, good from the first bite to the last.",
      "paragraph_id": 10,
      "word_count": 18,
      "start_time": 118.525,
      "end_time": 124.85,
      "duration": 6.325,
      "phoneme_count": 93
